.TH CHTTP_REQUEST_GET_HEADER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_request_get_header \- look up a request header by name
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

const char *chttp_request_get_header(const chttp_request_t *req,
                                     const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the stored value of the header with the name that
you give, or NULL if that header is not there. The lookup ignores the
case of the name: the function makes your name lowercase before the
lookup.

The pointer that the function gives back stays valid until the next
call to chttp_request_set_header on this request, or until somebody
frees the request.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
req   The request to query. It can be NULL, and the function then
      gives NULL.
name  The header name. It can be NULL, and the function then gives
      NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the stored value string, or NULL if the function does not
find that header.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_set_header (3)
